y Annual Report 2025-26 - Council 260722","url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80249/appendix-1-treasury-annual-report-2025-26-council-260722.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"22/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix A - ELDC Outturn 25.26 Finance Revenue Report - EB 260701","url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80129/appendix-a-eldc-outturn-25-26-finance-revenue-report-eb-2607.pdf","committee":"Executive Board","date":"01/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix B - ELDC Outturn 25.26 Finance Capital Report - EB 260701","url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80130/appendix-b-eldc-outturn-25-26-finance-capital-report-eb-2607.pdf","committee":"Executive Board","date":"01/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Treasury Annual Report 2025 26 - AG 260630","url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80144/treasury-annual-report-2025-26-ag-260630.pdf","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","date":"30/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"APPENDIX 1 - Treasury Annual Report 2025-26 - AG 260630","url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80145/appendix-1-treasury-annual-report-2025-26-ag-260630.pdf","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","date":"30/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Unaudited Financial Statements 2025 26 - AG 260630","url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80140/unaudited-financial-statements-2025-26-ag-260630.pdf","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","date":"30/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"APPENDIX 1 - ELDC - Unaudited Financial Statements 2025-26 - AG 260630","url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80141/appendix-1-eldc-unaudited-financial-statements-2025-26-ag-26.pdf","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","date":"30/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Draft Annual Governance Statement (AGS) 2025 26 - AG 260630","url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80142/draft-annual-governance-statement-ags-2025-26-ag-260630.pdf","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","date":"30/06/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Executive Board","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-17","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-06-30","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-01","committee":"Executive Board","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-22","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Investment income forecast to outperform budget by \u00a31.2m, heavily dependent on temporary rate environment","lead":"While the income boost improves the revenue account and cash position, it is vulnerable to reversal if the Bank of England cuts rates (currently at 3.75%) or if capital spending accelerates and depletes cash. The council's financial plan is dependent on\u2026","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"APPENDIX 1 - Q1 Treasury Report 2026-27 - AG 260909","paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80445/80445.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"No new borrowing anticipated despite \u00a338.8m capital budget","lead":"A local authority forecasting no borrowing need indicates sufficient liquidity and no external financing requirement, demonstrating financial resilience and that the council is managing within existing resources.","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"APPENDIX 1 - Q1 Treasury Report 2026-27 - AG 260909","paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80445/80445.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Capital programme slippage from 2025/26 has left higher cash balances available for investment than projected","lead":"Capital programme slippage indicates planned capital expenditure did not proceed as scheduled, which may reflect resource constraints, procurement delays, or project delivery issues. Lenders need to understand whether capital plans are realistic and\u2026","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Q1 Treasury Report 2026 27 - AG 260909","paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80444/80444.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"APPENDIX 1 - Q1 Treasury Report 2026-27 - AG 260909","paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80445/80445.pdf","headline":"Investment income forecast to outperform budget by \u00a31.2m, heavily dependent on temporary rate environment","detail":"The council budgeted for \u00a31.375m investment income but is forecasting \u00a32.599m outturn\u2014an outperformance of \u00a31.224m. This is explicitly attributed to higher interest rates than budgeted (treasury investments yielding 4.34%, property funds 3.86%) and higher cash balances from slippage in the prior year's capital programme.","category":"income","matters":"While the income boost improves the revenue account and cash position, it is vulnerable to reversal if the Bank of England cuts rates (currently at 3.75%) or if capital spending accelerates and depletes cash. The council's financial plan is dependent on temporary market conditions.","figures":"Budget \u00a31,375,200; forecast outturn \u00a32,599,084; favorable variance \u00a31,223,884; treasury yield 4.34%, property yield 3.86%","quote":"The higher level of investment income achieved compared to the original budget is due to interest rates in the market being higher than the budgeted return for 2026/27 and balances available for investment being higher due to slippage in the 2025/26 capital programme.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"APPENDIX 1 - Q1 Treasury Report 2026-27 - AG 260909","paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80445/80445.pdf","headline":"No new borrowing anticipated despite \u00a338.8m capital budget","detail":"The council expects to fund its 2026/27 capital programme entirely from existing resources without undertaking new long-term borrowing. This reflects strong cash generation and investment balances totalling \u00a362.6m at end of Q1.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A local authority forecasting no borrowing need indicates sufficient liquidity and no external financing requirement, demonstrating financial resilience and that the council is managing within existing resources.","figures":"Capital expenditure budget \u00a338.8m; investments held \u00a362.6m at Q1; no temporary borrowing outstanding","quote":"It is anticipated that new long term borrowing will not be undertaken during this financial year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Q1 Treasury Report 2026 27 - AG 260909","paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80444/80444.pdf","headline":"Capital programme slippage from 2025/26 has left higher cash balances available for investment than projected","detail":"The council achieved investment income of \u00a3503,706 in Q1 against a budget of \u00a3177,837, a favorable variance of \u00a3325,869. The council attributes this outperformance partly to higher interest rates and partly to 'balances available for investment being higher due to slippage in the capital programme from 2025/26'. The report does not specify the scale of the slippage, its underlying cause, or whether the capital spending is expected to be recovered.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital programme slippage indicates planned capital expenditure did not proceed as scheduled, which may reflect resource constraints, procurement delays, or project delivery issues. Lenders need to understand whether capital plans are realistic and executable, as slippage affects future borrowing requirements and cash flow.","figures":"Q1 investment income \u00a3503,706 actual vs \u00a3177,837 budget","quote":"balances available for investment being higher due to slippage in the capital programme from 2025/26","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"V3 ELDC Audit Governance Annual Report 2025 26 - Reviewed KB","paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80487/80487.pdf","headline":"Risk management framework does not provide confidence that risks are managed consistently and effectively","detail":"The Head of Internal Audit concluded that while the risk management framework was in place and subject to regular review, 'current arrangements did not provide confidence that risks were managed consistently and effectively.' The Committee noted that improvement was required to strengthen risk management practices.","category":"governance","matters":"Consistent and effective risk management is essential to financial stability and service delivery. If the council cannot reliably identify and manage emerging risks, exposures may be missed that could impact the council's financial position or ability to meet obligations.","figures":"Assessment from Internal Audit Annual Report and Opinion 2025/26 presentation, June 2026","quote":"However, current arrangements did not provide confidence that risks were managed consistently and effectively; the proposed improvements would help to further strengthen its maturity and consistency.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"V3 ELDC Audit Governance Annual Report 2025 26 - Reviewed KB","paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80487/80487.pdf","headline":"Internal audit identified Insufficient Controls relating to identification and monitoring of savings, described as 'extremely serious'","detail":"In September 2025, internal audit raised a finding of Insufficient Controls over the identification and monitoring of savings. The Audit and Governance Committee chairman described this as 'extremely serious' because there were not enough processes in place to determine whether this aspect of finances was being run well. The issue was repeated in Q4, indicating it remained a focus area throughout the year.","category":"savings","matters":"A lender requires confidence that a council can reliably track and implement savings plans, which are typically critical to maintaining financial stability. Insufficient controls over savings identification means the council cannot adequately verify that planned savings are being delivered.","figures":"Findings identified in Q1 and Q4 2025/26","quote":"Another challenge has been the audit finding in September of Insufficient Controls relating to the identification and monitoring of savings. This was an extremely serious matter, because internal audit identified that there weren't enough processes in place to be able to tell whether this aspect of finances was being run well or not.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-09"},"name":"East Lindsey","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"Investment income forecast to outperform budget by \u00a31.2m, heavily dependent on temporary rate environment","lead":"While the income boost improves the revenue account and cash position, it is vulnerable to reversal if the Bank of England cuts rates (currently at 3.75%) or if capital spending accelerates and depletes cash. The council's financial plan is dependent on\u2026","also":["4 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Executive Board on 2026-09-23","n_findings":5,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"APPENDIX 1 - Q1 Treasury Report 2026-27 - AG 260909","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.e-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s80445/80445.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":45,"news_drafts_total":3}}